  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has AAA silver coins and BBB gold coins.\n\nHe can avail the following 222 deals (multiple times):\n\n\nSell 111 silver coin for Rs. 111.\nTrade 111 gold coin for 222 silver coins.\nChef is trying to sell all his coins and earn money now. How much money will Chef be able to earn?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of each test case contains 222 integers - AAA and BBB.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the amount of money Chef can earn.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤A,B≤101 \\le A, B \\le 101≤A,B≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 1",
        "output": "4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef can first trade his gold coin for 222 silver coins. Now he has 444 silver coins in total, and he sells all of them for Rs. 444."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "10 10",
        "output": "30",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ]
  },
